IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `caa-types`
IMPORT `caa-convention-liability`

-- Tests for the Convention, Chapter III (Articles 17 to 30A), each against the Convention it
-- names.  Figures read off the text: the limits of Article 22 (125,000 and 250,000 francs; 250
-- francs and 17 SDR per kilogramme; 5,000 francs), the complaint periods of Article 26 (3, 7, 14
-- and 7, 14, 21 days), the two years of Article 29, the 6 months of Article 22(4).

§ `Tests -- Chapter III`

§§ `Article 17. Passenger`

-- Passenger Accident Facts: death or bodily injury, on board the aircraft, embarking or disembarking.
#ASSERT `the carrier is liable under Article 17` (`Passenger Accident Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE)
#ASSERT `the carrier is liable under Article 17` (`Passenger Accident Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the carrier is liable under Article 17` (`Passenger Accident Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the carrier is liable under Article 17` (`Passenger Accident Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE)

§§ `Article 18. Baggage and cargo`

-- Cargo Loss Facts: baggage damage, cargo damage, occurrence during the carriage by air, in the carrier's charge,
-- occurrence in carriage by land, sea or river outside an aerodrome, in performance of a contract for carriage by air,
-- proof to the contrary, then (Third Schedule) solely from an inherent defect, defective packaging, war, public authority.
`baggage in the carrier's charge` MEANS `Cargo Loss Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`cargo lost during the carriage by air` MEANS `Cargo Loss Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`cargo damaged outside the carriage by air` MEANS `Cargo Loss Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`cargo damaged on a road transfer for loading` MEANS `Cargo Loss Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`the same, where there is proof to the contrary` MEANS `Cargo Loss Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`cargo damaged on a road journey not for loading or delivery` MEANS `Cargo Loss Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`cargo lost solely from an inherent defect` MEANS `Cargo Loss Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`cargo lost solely from defective packaging by another` MEANS `Cargo Loss Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE
`cargo lost solely from an act of war` MEANS `Cargo Loss Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE
`cargo lost solely from an act of public authority` MEANS `Cargo Loss Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`baggage lost with an inherent-defect finding` MEANS `Cargo Loss Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT `the carrier is liable under Article 18` `the Warsaw Convention` `baggage in the carrier's charge`
#ASSERT `the carrier is liable under Article 18` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `baggage in the carrier's charge`
#ASSERT `the carrier is liable under Article 18` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `baggage in the carrier's charge`
#ASSERT `the carrier is liable under Article 18` `the Warsaw Convention` `cargo lost during the carriage by air`
#ASSERT NOT `the carrier is liable under Article 18` `the Warsaw Convention` `cargo damaged outside the carriage by air`
#ASSERT `the carrier is liable under Article 18` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `cargo damaged on a road transfer for loading`
#ASSERT `the damage is presumed to have resulted from an event during the carriage by air` `cargo damaged on a road transfer for loading`
#ASSERT NOT `the carrier is liable under Article 18` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `the same, where there is proof to the contrary`
#ASSERT NOT `the carrier is liable under Article 18` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `cargo damaged on a road journey not for loading or delivery`
-- the Third Schedule's four exceptions, for cargo only, and only where the loss resulted solely from them
#ASSERT `the carrier is liable under Article 18` `the Warsaw Convention` `cargo lost solely from an inherent defect`
#ASSERT `the carrier is liable under Article 18` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `cargo lost solely from an inherent defect`
#ASSERT NOT `the carrier is liable under Article 18` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `cargo lost solely from an inherent defect`
#ASSERT NOT `the carrier is liable under Article 18` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `cargo lost solely from defective packaging by another`
#ASSERT NOT `the carrier is liable under Article 18` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `cargo lost solely from an act of war`
#ASSERT NOT `the carrier is liable under Article 18` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `cargo lost solely from an act of public authority`
#ASSERT `the carrier is liable under Article 18` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `baggage lost with an inherent-defect finding`

§§ `Article 19. Delay`

#ASSERT `the carrier is liable under Article 19` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the carrier is liable under Article 19` FALSE

§§ `Article 20. Defence`

-- Defence Facts: took all necessary measures, impossible, negligent pilotage, all other measures taken.
`the carrier took all necessary measures` MEANS `Defence Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`it was impossible to take measures` MEANS `Defence Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE
`negligent pilotage, all else done` MEANS `Defence Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE
`negligent pilotage, not all else done` MEANS `Defence Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE
`no defence` MEANS `Defence Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT `the carrier is not liable by reason of Article 20` `the Warsaw Convention` `the destruction or loss of, or damage to, cargo` `the carrier took all necessary measures`
#ASSERT `the carrier is not liable by reason of Article 20` `the Warsaw Convention` `the destruction or loss of, or damage to, cargo` `it was impossible to take measures`
#ASSERT `the carrier is not liable by reason of Article 20` `the Warsaw Convention` `the destruction or loss of, or damage to, cargo` `negligent pilotage, all else done`
#ASSERT NOT `the carrier is not liable by reason of Article 20` `the Warsaw Convention` `the destruction or loss of, or damage to, cargo` `negligent pilotage, not all else done`
-- Article 20(2) (Second Schedule) is for cargo and baggage, not for a passenger's injury
#ASSERT NOT `the carrier is not liable by reason of Article 20` `the Warsaw Convention` `the death or wounding of a passenger or other bodily injury to a passenger` `negligent pilotage, all else done`
#ASSERT `the carrier is not liable by reason of Article 20` `the Warsaw Convention` `the death or wounding of a passenger or other bodily injury to a passenger` `the carrier took all necessary measures`
#ASSERT NOT `the carrier is not liable by reason of Article 20` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `the destruction or loss of, or damage to, cargo` `negligent pilotage, all else done`
#ASSERT `the carrier is not liable by reason of Article 20` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `the destruction or loss of, or damage to, cargo` `the carrier took all necessary measures`
#ASSERT `the carrier is not liable by reason of Article 20` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `the death or wounding of a passenger or other bodily injury to a passenger` `the carrier took all necessary measures`
#ASSERT `the carrier is not liable by reason of Article 20` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `the destruction or loss of, or damage to, registered baggage` `it was impossible to take measures`
#ASSERT `the carrier is not liable by reason of Article 20` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `delay in the carriage by air of passengers, baggage or cargo` `the carrier took all necessary measures`
-- Third Schedule: no Article 20 defence for the destruction, loss or damage of cargo
#ASSERT NOT `the carrier is not liable by reason of Article 20` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `the destruction or loss of, or damage to, cargo` `the carrier took all necessary measures`
#ASSERT NOT `the carrier is not liable by reason of Article 20` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `the destruction or loss of, or damage to, registered baggage` `no defence`

§§ `Article 21. Contributory negligence`

-- Contributory Negligence Facts: the person suffering the damage was negligent; the claimant was negligent or wrongful.
`the injured person was negligent` MEANS `Contributory Negligence Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE
`the cargo claimant was at fault` MEANS `Contributory Negligence Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE
`no fault` MEANS `Contributory Negligence Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT `the court may exonerate the carrier wholly or partly` `the Warsaw Convention` `a passenger` `the injured person was negligent`
#ASSERT `the court may exonerate the carrier wholly or partly` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `cargo` `the injured person was negligent`
#ASSERT `the court may exonerate the carrier wholly or partly` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `a passenger` `the injured person was negligent`
#ASSERT `the court may exonerate the carrier wholly or partly` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `registered baggage` `the injured person was negligent`
#ASSERT NOT `the court may exonerate the carrier wholly or partly` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `cargo` `the injured person was negligent`
#ASSERT NOT `the court may exonerate the carrier wholly or partly` `the Warsaw Convention` `a passenger` `no fault`
-- Article 21(2) (Third Schedule): for cargo the carrier "shall be" exonerated to the extent of the claimant's fault
#ASSERT `the carrier must be exonerated to the extent the claimant's fault caused or contributed to the damage` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `cargo` `the cargo claimant was at fault`
#ASSERT NOT `the carrier must be exonerated to the extent the claimant's fault caused or contributed to the damage` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `cargo` `no fault`
#ASSERT NOT `the carrier must be exonerated to the extent the claimant's fault caused or contributed to the damage` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `a passenger` `the cargo claimant was at fault`
#ASSERT NOT `the carrier must be exonerated to the extent the claimant's fault caused or contributed to the damage` `the Warsaw Convention` `cargo` `the cargo claimant was at fault`
#ASSERT NOT `the carrier must be exonerated to the extent the claimant's fault caused or contributed to the damage` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `cargo` `the cargo claimant was at fault`

§§ `Article 22. Limits`

-- the limits themselves, each Schedule
#ASSERT (`the liability limit under Article 22` `the Warsaw Convention` `the liability for each passenger in the carriage of persons`)'s `the amount` EQUALS 125_000
#ASSERT (`the liability limit under Article 22` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `the liability for each passenger in the carriage of persons`)'s `the amount` EQUALS 250_000
#ASSERT (`the liability limit under Article 22` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `the liability for each passenger in the carriage of persons`)'s `the amount` EQUALS 250_000
#ASSERT (`the liability limit under Article 22` `the Warsaw Convention` `the liability for registered baggage`)'s `the amount` EQUALS 250
#ASSERT (`the liability limit under Article 22` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `the liability for registered baggage`)'s `the amount` EQUALS 250
#ASSERT (`the liability limit under Article 22` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `the liability for registered baggage`)'s `the amount` EQUALS 250
#ASSERT (`the liability limit under Article 22` `the Warsaw Convention` `the liability for cargo`)'s `the amount` EQUALS 250
#ASSERT (`the liability limit under Article 22` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `the liability for cargo`)'s `the amount` EQUALS 250
#ASSERT (`the liability limit under Article 22` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `the liability for cargo`)'s `the amount` EQUALS 17
#ASSERT (`the liability limit under Article 22` `the Warsaw Convention` `the liability for objects of which the passenger takes charge himself`)'s `the amount` EQUALS 5_000
#ASSERT (`the liability limit under Article 22` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `the liability for objects of which the passenger takes charge himself`)'s `the amount` EQUALS 5_000
-- the units
#ASSERT (`the liability limit under Article 22` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `the liability for cargo`)'s `the unit` EQUALS `Special Drawing Rights`
#ASSERT (`the liability limit under Article 22` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `the liability for cargo`)'s `the unit` EQUALS Francs
#ASSERT (`the liability limit under Article 22` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `the liability for registered baggage`)'s `the unit` EQUALS Francs
#ASSERT (`the liability limit under Article 22` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `the liability for each passenger in the carriage of persons`)'s `the unit` EQUALS Francs
-- per kilogramme for baggage and cargo, not for passengers or objects the passenger holds
#ASSERT (`the liability limit under Article 22` `the Warsaw Convention` `the liability for cargo`)'s `the amount is per kilogramme`
#ASSERT (`the liability limit under Article 22` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `the liability for registered baggage`)'s `the amount is per kilogramme`
#ASSERT NOT (`the liability limit under Article 22` `the Warsaw Convention` `the liability for each passenger in the carriage of persons`)'s `the amount is per kilogramme`
#ASSERT NOT (`the liability limit under Article 22` `the Warsaw Convention` `the liability for objects of which the passenger takes charge himself`)'s `the amount is per kilogramme`

-- the amount for a claim.  Limit Facts: special contract for a higher limit, the higher limit, special declaration and any
-- supplementary sum paid, the declared sum, the carrier proves the declared sum exceeds the actual interest, the actual
-- interest, weight of the packages concerned in kilogrammes, part affects the value of other packages, weight of those.
`a passenger with no special contract` MEANS `Limit Facts` OF FALSE, 0,       FALSE, 0,     FALSE, 0,     0,  FALSE, 0
`a passenger with a special contract for 400000 francs` MEANS `Limit Facts` OF TRUE,  400_000, FALSE, 0,     FALSE, 0,     0,  FALSE, 0
`10 kilogrammes with no declaration` MEANS `Limit Facts` OF FALSE, 0,       FALSE, 0,     FALSE, 0,     10, FALSE, 0
`100 kilogrammes with no declaration` MEANS `Limit Facts` OF FALSE, 0,       FALSE, 0,     FALSE, 0,     100, FALSE, 0
`10 kilogrammes declared at 3000` MEANS `Limit Facts` OF FALSE, 0,       TRUE,  3_000, FALSE, 0,     10, FALSE, 0
`10 kilogrammes declared at 3000, actual interest proved to be 2000` MEANS `Limit Facts` OF FALSE, 0,       TRUE,  3_000, TRUE,  2_000, 10, FALSE, 0
`10 kilogrammes, loss of part affecting 5 kilogrammes of other packages` MEANS `Limit Facts` OF FALSE, 0,       FALSE, 0,     FALSE, 0,     10, TRUE,  5

