#ASSERT NOT `the court may award costs and other expenses of the litigation in addition to the limit` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `damages of 90 after an offer of 100 made in time`
#ASSERT `the court may award costs and other expenses of the litigation in addition to the limit` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `damages of 150 after an offer of 100 made in time`
#ASSERT `the court may award costs and other expenses of the litigation in addition to the limit` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `damages of 100 after an offer of 100 made after 6 months and after the action`
#ASSERT `the court may award costs and other expenses of the litigation in addition to the limit` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `damages of 100 with no offer`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the court may award costs and other expenses of the litigation in addition to the limit` `the Warsaw Convention` `damages of 100 with no offer`

§§ `Article 23. Contractual provisions`

-- Clause Facts: tends to relieve the carrier or fix a lower limit, inherent-defect provision, then Article 32 fields.
`a clause excluding liability` MEANS `Clause Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a clause about inherent defect of cargo` MEANS `Clause Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a clause that does not affect liability` MEANS `Clause Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT `the provision is null and void under Article 23` `the Warsaw Convention` `a clause excluding liability`
#ASSERT `the provision is null and void under Article 23` `the Warsaw Convention` `a clause about inherent defect of cargo`
#ASSERT `the provision is null and void under Article 23` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `a clause excluding liability`
#ASSERT NOT `the provision is null and void under Article 23` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `a clause about inherent defect of cargo`
#ASSERT NOT `the provision is null and void under Article 23` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `a clause about inherent defect of cargo`
#ASSERT NOT `the provision is null and void under Article 23` `the Warsaw Convention` `a clause that does not affect liability`
#ASSERT NOT `the nullity of such a provision involves the nullity of the whole contract of carriage`

§§ `Article 24. Exclusivity`

#ASSERT `an action for damages can only be brought subject to the conditions and limits of the Convention` `the death or wounding of a passenger or other bodily injury to a passenger`
#ASSERT `an action for damages can only be brought subject to the conditions and limits of the Convention` `the destruction or loss of, or damage to, registered baggage`
#ASSERT `an action for damages can only be brought subject to the conditions and limits of the Convention` `the destruction or loss of, or damage to, cargo`
#ASSERT `an action for damages can only be brought subject to the conditions and limits of the Convention` `delay in the carriage by air of passengers, baggage or cargo`
#ASSERT `the limits of liability are maximum limits that may not be exceeded whatever the circumstances` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `cargo`
#ASSERT NOT `the limits of liability are maximum limits that may not be exceeded whatever the circumstances` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `a passenger`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the limits of liability are maximum limits that may not be exceeded whatever the circumstances` `the Warsaw Convention` `cargo`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the limits of liability are maximum limits that may not be exceeded whatever the circumstances` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `cargo`

§§ `Article 25. Loss of the benefit of the limits`

-- Limit Breaking Facts: carrier's intent or recklessness, a servant's such act, within employment, wilful misconduct,
-- equivalent default, so caused by a servant or agent within employment.
`intent by the carrier` MEANS `Limit Breaking Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`recklessness by a servant within employment` MEANS `Limit Breaking Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`recklessness by a servant outside employment` MEANS `Limit Breaking Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`wilful misconduct by the carrier` MEANS `Limit Breaking Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE
`a default equivalent to wilful misconduct` MEANS `Limit Breaking Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE
`wilful misconduct by a servant within employment` MEANS `Limit Breaking Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`no misconduct` MEANS `Limit Breaking Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `the limits of liability apply` `the Warsaw Convention` `a passenger` `wilful misconduct by the carrier`
#ASSERT NOT `the limits of liability apply` `the Warsaw Convention` `registered baggage` `a default equivalent to wilful misconduct`
#ASSERT NOT `the limits of liability apply` `the Warsaw Convention` `cargo` `wilful misconduct by a servant within employment`
#ASSERT `the limits of liability apply` `the Warsaw Convention` `a passenger` `no misconduct`
#ASSERT `the limits of liability apply` `the Warsaw Convention` `a passenger` `intent by the carrier`
#ASSERT NOT `the limits of liability apply` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `a passenger` `intent by the carrier`
#ASSERT NOT `the limits of liability apply` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `cargo` `intent by the carrier`
#ASSERT NOT `the limits of liability apply` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `cargo` `recklessness by a servant within employment`
#ASSERT `the limits of liability apply` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `cargo` `recklessness by a servant outside employment`
#ASSERT `the limits of liability apply` `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention` `cargo` `wilful misconduct by the carrier`
-- Third Schedule: the limits are lost for passengers and baggage, never for cargo (Article 24(2))
#ASSERT NOT `the limits of liability apply` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `a passenger` `intent by the carrier`
#ASSERT NOT `the limits of liability apply` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `registered baggage` `recklessness by a servant within employment`
#ASSERT `the limits of liability apply` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `cargo` `intent by the carrier`
#ASSERT `the limits of liability apply` `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention` `registered baggage` `recklessness by a servant outside employment`

